%---------------- ISPF Tutorial 2 of 5: Dynamic Areas --------------------%
%Command ===>_ZCMD
+
 ULS uses an AREA(DYNAMIC) field. The exec builds fixed-width records
 containing a data set name, volume, migration flag, and device.
+
 The panel binds that field to DYNAREA and DYNSHAD. Each row begins
 with an attribute byte so the exec can choose its display color.
 The shadow data marks the action column as an input field, allowing a
 B, E, V, or I selection on each displayed row.
+
 The exec rebuilds the visible slice before DISPLAY. Scroll verbs and
 the UP/DOWN commands move the first row; the dynamic area then shows
 the new slice.
+
 Enter NEXT, PREV, 1-5, or END to navigate.
)END
